.TH CSTRING_RESERVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_reserve \- pre-allocate capacity for at least min_capacity bytes
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

bool cstring_reserve(cstr s, size_t min_capacity);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Ensures the internal buffer has room for at least min_capacity bytes
(including the null terminator). The requested size is rounded up to the
nearest power of two (minimum 16). Does nothing if the current capacity
already satisfies the request.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s              String to modify
min_capacity   Minimum number of bytes to reserve (including null terminator)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
true on success or if capacity was already sufficient
false if reallocation failed or the requested size is too large
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_create_full (3)
